# Sphere-local Caddy routes — imported by the upstream Caddyfile (`import sphere.caddy`).
#
# Sphere-owned: the upstream template ships this empty stub and never edits it, so it
# never conflicts on `git merge` (also pinned `merge=ours` in .gitattributes).
# Add THIS sphere's extra gateway routes here instead of editing the Caddyfile, so
# upstream improvements to the base Caddyfile keep flowing in cleanly.
#
# These tokens are injected inside the `:80 { ... }` site block, before the static
# catch-all. Example — proxy an extra backend path to Odoo:
#
#   @sphere_api path /myapi/*
#   handle @sphere_api {
#       reverse_proxy odoo:8069
#   }
